<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard an Iarainn Bourke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1583">1583</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Iron Dick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard an Iarainn Bourke, called 'Iron Dick', was a Gaelicised Burke lord of Mayo who became The Mac William Íochtar in 1580. He was the second husband of the sea captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grace-omalley">Grace O'Malley</a>, and their son was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theobald-bourke-1st-viscount-mayo">Tibbot na Long</a> Bourke. He rebelled against the English in 1580 but soon made his peace, was knighted in 1581 and died in 1583.</p></div>
